      "title": "Course creators: captions as a starting point for lesson notes",
      "copy": "Course creators: an existing subtitle file can also be a useful starting point for lesson notes.\n\nChoose the export for the job:\n\n• Plain transcript: text to edit into reading notes.\n• Timed transcript: text with timestamps so you can find a passage in the lesson.\n• CSV cue sheet: a table for reviewing individual cues and timings.\n\nKeep the original SRT/VTT for video playback. Review the words against the lesson and edit the transcript before sharing it; converting a file does not check accuracy or turn it into finished notes.\n\nI’m the seller of Caption Cleanup Kit. It exports these formats from existing UTF-8 SRT/VTT files in an offline desktop-browser workspace. US$9 once, including a quick-start guide and samples. No subtitle uploads or subscription. It does not transcribe audio or translate speech.\n\nhttps://tiaanbok0.gumroad.com/l/caption-cleanup-kit?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=transcripts20261013\n\n#CourseCreation #Subtitles",
